\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Lord, Thy word abideth,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And our footsteps guideth:
\par Who is truth believeth
\par Light and joy receiveth.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When our foes are near us,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Then Thy word doth cheer us,
\par Word of consolation,
\par Message of salvation.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When the storms are o'er us,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And dark clouds before us,
\par Then its light directeth,
\par And our way protecteth.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4. Who can tell the pleasure,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Who recount the treasure,
\par By Thy word imparted
\par To the simple-hearted?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   5. Word of mercy, giving
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Succour to the living;
\par Word of life, supplying
\par Comfort to the dying!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6. O that we, discerning
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Its most holy learning,
\par Lord, may love and fear Thee,
\par \pard     Evermore be near Thee!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

